    "cohabit": {
      "word": "COHABIT",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To inhabit or reside in company, or in the same place or country. The Philistines were worsted by the captived ark . . . : they were not able to cohabit with that holy thing. South.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To dwell or live together as husband and wife. The law presumes that husband and wife cohabit together, even after a voluntary separation has taken place between them. Bouvier. presumed when a man and woman cohabit permanently together, being reputed by those who know them to be husband and wife, and admitting the relationship. Wharton.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
